        "original_id": "6d2d3f53-5415-5536-962a-7f71bd1d0978",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Elgin Theatre, Ottawa, Ontario, Canada, Lisgar and Elgin Street\n- People: Mary Pickford, Douglas Fairbanks, Charlie Chaplin, D.W. Griffith\n- Organizations: Pickford-Fairbanks Studio, United Artists, Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences\n- Events: world premiere of \"Sleep, My Love\"\n\nFacts:\n- The Elgin Theatre was a historic movie theatre at the corner of Lisgar and Elgin Street in Ottawa, Ontario, Canada.\n- For several decades, the Elgin Theatre was one of Ottawa's premier theatres.\n- In 1947, the Elgin Theatre hosted the world premiere of Mary Pickford's \"Sleep, My Love\".\n- Mary Pickford co-founded the Pickford-Fairbanks Studio with Douglas Fairbanks.\n- Mary Pickford later co-founded United Artists with Douglas Fairbanks, Charlie Chaplin, and D.W. Griffith.\n- Mary Pickford was one of the original 36 founders of the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences, which presents the annual Oscar awards.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
